1.GET SMALLER ELEMENTS 
Given an array arr, return all the elements which are less than a given value x. The order of returned smaller elements should be according their appearance in the input array. 
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static ArrayList<Integer> getSmaller(int arr[], int target) {
                ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]<target){
                        list.add(arr[i]);
                    }
                }
                return list;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/get-smaller-elements/1


2.COUNT OF DIGIT K IN ARRAY : 
Given an array arr[]. Your task is to return an integer denoting the total number of times digit k appears in the array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int countDigitK(int k, int arr[]) {
                int count=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    while(arr[i]>0){
                        int div=arr[i]%10;
                        if(div==k){
                            count++;
                        }
                        arr[i]/=10;
                    }
                }
                return count;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-number-of-numbers/1


3.INDEX OF AN EXTRA ELEMENT 
You have given two sorted arrays a[] & b[] of distinct elements. The first array has one element extra added in between. Return the index of the extra element.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int findExtra(int a[], int b[]) {
                int low=0;
                int high=b.length-1;
                int ans=a.length-1;
                while(low<=high){
                    int mid=low+(high-low)/2;
                    if(a[mid]==b[mid]){
                        low=mid+1;
                    }
                    else{
                        ans=mid;
                        high=mid-1;
                    }
                }
                return ans;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/index-of-an-extra-element/1


4.ROOF TOP 
You are given and array arr[] representing the heights of n consecutive buildings. You can move from the roof of a building to the roof of the next adjacent building. 
You need to find the maximum number of consecutive steps you can put forward such that every step is to a higher building than the previous one. 
SOURCE CODE : 
class Solution {
    public int maxStep(int arr[]) {
        int count=0;
        int maxCount=0;
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){
            if(arr[i]<arr[i+1]){
                count++;
                maxCount=Math.max(maxCount,count);
            }
            else{
                count=0;
            }
        }
        return maxCount;
    }
}
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/roof-top-1587115621/1


5.NEXT PRIME NUMBER 
Given an integer n. Write a program to find the first prime number greater than n.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static int nextPrime(int n) {
                for(int i=n+1;i<=500;i++){
                    boolean isprime=true;
                    for(int j=2;j<=Math.sqrt(i);j++){
                        if(i%j==0){
                            isprime=false;
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                    if(isprime){
                        return i;
                    }
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/next-prime-number/1
